WEBVTT

00:00:10.990 --> 00:00:13.660
Keyaki Park Ice Arena

00:00:13.660 --> 00:00:16.330
Let's practice doing it together a little!

00:00:16.330 --> 00:00:18.370
We don't have much time before the match!

00:00:18.370 --> 00:00:20.740
We haven't decided on a piece,
or routine, or positions yet.

00:00:20.740 --> 00:00:22.490
There's nothing to practice together.

00:00:22.490 --> 00:00:24.160
Yeah, yeah!

00:00:24.160 --> 00:00:26.160
Also, watch how you talk to me.

00:00:26.160 --> 00:00:28.240
I'll beat you up!

00:00:28.240 --> 00:00:29.580
Hey, wait!

00:00:29.580 --> 00:00:31.200
I'm not done talking yet!

00:00:31.200 --> 00:00:32.870
Club practice is over.

00:00:32.870 --> 00:00:34.080
What?

00:00:34.080 --> 00:00:36.910
Jeez, what're we supposed to do?

00:00:36.910 --> 00:00:39.240
The match is this weekend!

00:00:39.240 --> 00:00:40.660
Yeah, it is.

00:00:40.660 --> 00:00:42.410
Think about it properly!

00:00:42.410 --> 00:00:44.040
I'm thinking right now.

00:00:44.040 --> 00:00:46.620
The piece, routine, positions, practice--

00:00:46.620 --> 00:00:49.490
There's so much we still have to do,
but nothing's been decided!

00:00:49.490 --> 00:00:51.740
We're up against last year's
national semifinalists,

00:00:51.740 --> 00:00:53.950
and we're dropping out if we lose!

00:00:53.950 --> 00:00:55.290
Well, you know.

00:00:55.290 --> 00:00:58.620
If worst comes to worst, we can transfer
to another school. The two of us.

00:00:58.620 --> 00:01:00.040
What?!

00:01:00.040 --> 00:01:02.080
What the hell are you thinking?

00:01:02.080 --> 00:01:03.240
<i>You're</i> the one

00:01:03.240 --> 00:01:06.870
who was acting all cool and talking about
"bringing this team together" before!

00:01:06.870 --> 00:01:08.620
I'm just kidding.

00:01:08.620 --> 00:01:12.790
In order to beat Shinozaki, this is
the best team, with these members.

00:01:12.790 --> 00:01:14.490
I won't give that up.

00:01:14.490 --> 00:01:16.740
Huh?

00:02:52.020 --> 00:02:55.540
Episode 2

00:02:52.020 --> 00:02:55.540
Self-Centered

00:02:59.080 --> 00:03:00.200
Hayato.

00:03:01.200 --> 00:03:02.290
Where are we?

00:03:02.290 --> 00:03:04.370
Huh?

00:03:04.370 --> 00:03:05.540
I got separated.

00:03:05.540 --> 00:03:08.160
Hey, was this guy always like that?

00:03:08.160 --> 00:03:10.660
I thought he spoke more, like, clearly.

00:03:10.660 --> 00:03:11.870
How should I know?

00:03:11.870 --> 00:03:14.080
We've never been close or anything.

00:03:14.080 --> 00:03:16.950
He's always been an annoying bastard
who doesn't talk much, though.

00:03:16.950 --> 00:03:20.200
Transfer schools. I heard you say that.

00:03:20.200 --> 00:03:21.490
What is that about?

00:03:21.490 --> 00:03:22.330
Bleh!

00:03:22.330 --> 00:03:26.370
That was about us. It has nothing
to do with you, you know?

00:03:26.370 --> 00:03:30.120
I heard you ran away from home.
Now you're transferring?

00:03:30.120 --> 00:03:31.660
It's my life.

00:03:31.660 --> 00:03:35.120
I can live however I want, right? Big Bro.

00:03:37.290 --> 00:03:41.990
Uh, Shinozaki... Um, I'm back--on the ice.

00:03:41.990 --> 00:03:43.410
I know.

00:03:43.410 --> 00:03:47.700
Uh, I'm not breaking my promise with you.

00:03:47.700 --> 00:03:52.450
The promise was about singles, right?
And this is skate-leading.

00:03:52.450 --> 00:03:56.620
So, um... we'll be fighting again,
but this time--

00:03:56.620 --> 00:03:58.870
Hayato, go back home immediately.

00:03:58.870 --> 00:04:00.740
With your actions, so many people have--

00:04:00.740 --> 00:04:05.580
Will you please not ignore someone
speaking to you, Master Shinozaki?

00:04:05.580 --> 00:04:08.080
I don't know how famous you've become,

00:04:08.080 --> 00:04:09.790
but if you don't look over here
a little more carefully,

00:04:09.790 --> 00:04:12.580
then you'll lose to me in a second.

00:04:12.580 --> 00:04:17.120
People say that, but no one's
ever beat me before.

00:04:17.120 --> 00:04:18.370
Maeshima!

00:04:23.120 --> 00:04:24.240
Ah, wait!

00:04:24.240 --> 00:04:26.040
Wait, please wait!

00:04:26.040 --> 00:04:28.450
I'm sorry. I don't know what happened,

00:04:28.450 --> 00:04:31.160
but he's not doing it out of spite--

00:04:31.160 --> 00:04:32.290
Huh? Maeshima?

00:04:32.290 --> 00:04:33.580
Huh?

00:04:33.580 --> 00:04:34.620
Kurayoshi...

00:04:34.620 --> 00:04:36.450
I've been looking for you!

00:04:36.450 --> 00:04:39.790
Sorry about that. We'll be going, then.

00:04:39.790 --> 00:04:42.580
Right... Sorry from us, too...

00:04:42.580 --> 00:04:43.700
Oh, damn it!

00:04:43.700 --> 00:04:45.330
Huh?

00:04:45.330 --> 00:04:47.120
Give me some time alone.

00:04:47.120 --> 00:04:48.180
I'll be back the day after tomorrow.

00:04:48.180 --> 00:04:48.830
Huh?

00:04:48.830 --> 00:04:50.700
Make sure you keep practicing until then.

00:04:50.700 --> 00:04:52.120
Wait a minute!

00:04:52.120 --> 00:04:54.620
Also, don't get too carried away.

00:04:54.620 --> 00:04:55.620
Wha...?

00:05:03.790 --> 00:05:05.620
Ken, you look scary.

00:05:05.620 --> 00:05:08.540
I'm annoyed by a bunch of stuff.
Shinozaki, that bastard...

00:05:08.540 --> 00:05:10.370
Huh? Shinozaki?

00:05:10.370 --> 00:05:13.080
Hurry up and eat so we can practice! Practice!

00:05:13.080 --> 00:05:15.040
Oh, Jonouchi, sir.

00:05:15.040 --> 00:05:16.450
Hey, see you later.

00:05:16.450 --> 00:05:20.660
We'll practice during lunch, too,
so hurry up and eat, Jonouchi.

00:05:23.450 --> 00:05:25.950
Huh?

00:05:25.950 --> 00:05:27.450
What was that just now?

00:05:27.450 --> 00:05:29.120
Did you fight with Jonouchi and Himekawa?

00:05:29.120 --> 00:05:29.640
Aki.

00:05:29.640 --> 00:05:31.290
You can call me "Akimitsu, sir"

00:05:31.290 --> 00:05:33.120
or "Mochizuki, sir."

00:05:33.120 --> 00:05:36.290
You're a high schooler now, so you
should know to be respectful, right?

00:05:36.290 --> 00:05:40.160
I don't dislike you and Sasugai, you know.

00:05:40.160 --> 00:05:44.290
We're on the same team now,
so I'd like everyone to get along.

00:05:44.290 --> 00:05:45.580
Do your best.

00:05:45.580 --> 00:05:47.040
Akimitsu, sir...

00:05:47.040 --> 00:05:49.370
But you're amazing, Maeshima.

00:05:49.370 --> 00:05:50.740
Huh? Why?

00:05:50.740 --> 00:05:52.830
You don't worry about how many
calories you're eating at all.

00:05:52.830 --> 00:05:53.830
You're not the kind of guy that cares, huh?

00:05:53.830 --> 00:05:54.910
Huh?

00:06:01.290 --> 00:06:04.700
Th-This is how I've always been...

00:06:04.700 --> 00:06:07.660
Okay, Maeshima, look this way!

00:06:09.660 --> 00:06:10.490
Hey.

00:06:10.490 --> 00:06:14.450
I'll write that I've got a cute new
underclassman on my account.

00:06:14.450 --> 00:06:15.540
Oh, don't worry.

00:06:15.540 --> 00:06:19.490
Even if you drop out, the only people
who look at this are my fans.

00:06:19.490 --> 00:06:20.440
So you don't have to care about it.

00:06:20.440 --> 00:06:22.290
Crap, I wanna punch him...

00:06:22.290 --> 00:06:23.160
Please don't.

00:06:23.160 --> 00:06:26.330
"On this day, all my friends
seem more remarkable than I"...

00:06:26.330 --> 00:06:29.080
"My tears drench my face, as I f-frolic," uh...

00:06:29.080 --> 00:06:30.870
That's not it, Ken.

00:06:32.200 --> 00:06:33.410
Well, <i>sorry</i> !

00:06:32.910 --> 00:06:33.780
Ken!

00:06:33.910 --> 00:06:35.830
Put away your tray!

00:06:43.240 --> 00:06:44.910
So this is where you were.

00:06:44.910 --> 00:06:48.080
I needed to finish an assignment.

00:06:48.080 --> 00:06:50.790
You really are good at anything
thrown at you, aren't you?

00:06:50.790 --> 00:06:53.120
Are you saying I'm a Jack of all trades
and master of none?

00:06:53.120 --> 00:06:55.700
I didn't even think that.

00:06:55.700 --> 00:06:58.330
I'm bad with technology, anyway.

00:06:58.330 --> 00:06:58.430
Figure Skating
Grand Prix Series - Order List

00:06:58.330 --> 00:07:00.330
More importantly, what should we do for this?

00:06:58.430 --> 00:07:02.150
Figure Skating
Grand Prix Series - Order List

00:07:00.330 --> 00:07:02.740
This is this entry form
for the Grand Prix Series.

00:07:02.740 --> 00:07:03.620
For the members...

00:07:03.620 --> 00:07:06.490
Nothing will be decided until after the match.

00:07:08.080 --> 00:07:11.580
Shima might not be here by then...

00:07:11.580 --> 00:07:13.830
He'll get what he deserves.

00:07:13.830 --> 00:07:15.120
But...

00:07:15.120 --> 00:07:18.080
Won't <i>he</i> say something to him first?

00:07:18.080 --> 00:07:20.200
Words from our hero.

00:07:23.290 --> 00:07:26.370
Tomo, hurry up! Let's practice!

00:07:26.370 --> 00:07:27.990
W-Wait, Ken!

00:07:32.790 --> 00:07:34.200
Terauchi, sir.

00:07:34.200 --> 00:07:36.870
Maeshima, you're too self-centered.

00:07:36.870 --> 00:07:37.910
Huh?

00:07:37.910 --> 00:07:40.580
You move too much and build too much muscle.

00:07:40.580 --> 00:07:42.370
You aren't careful about what you eat.

00:07:42.370 --> 00:07:44.660
You rely completely on feeling when you skate.

00:07:44.660 --> 00:07:47.120
There's no way you can win like that.

00:07:47.120 --> 00:07:49.950
We're using the routine
we skated at nationals last year

00:07:49.950 --> 00:07:52.950
arranged for three people.

00:07:52.950 --> 00:07:55.700
Skate-leading is a team sport.

00:07:55.700 --> 00:07:57.450
What do you want to do?

00:07:57.450 --> 00:07:59.700
What can you do for the team?

00:07:59.700 --> 00:08:03.540
If you don't understand that,
even if you win the match,

00:08:03.540 --> 00:08:06.540
there won't be a place for you
on the starting team, Maeshima.

00:08:06.540 --> 00:08:07.870
Sho!

00:08:13.580 --> 00:08:16.490
Yo, how's practice going?

00:08:16.490 --> 00:08:17.580
Sasugai!

00:08:17.580 --> 00:08:20.120
Huh? I thought you weren't
coming back until tomorrow...?

00:08:20.120 --> 00:08:22.490
I finished earlier than expected.

00:08:22.490 --> 00:08:23.790
Where are the other two?

00:08:23.790 --> 00:08:28.080
Himekawa practiced on his own and then
decided when practice was over on his own.

00:08:28.080 --> 00:08:31.290
Jonouchi also said something
about not feeling motivated...

00:08:31.290 --> 00:08:33.540
Jeez, what am I gonna do with those guys--

00:08:33.540 --> 00:08:35.990
More importantly, where'd you go?

00:08:35.990 --> 00:08:36.990
Osaka.

00:08:36.990 --> 00:08:38.040
Huh?!

00:08:38.040 --> 00:08:39.540
I'll tell you the details later.

00:08:39.540 --> 00:08:41.870
First, take a look at this.

00:08:44.620 --> 00:08:45.790
What are you doing?

00:08:45.790 --> 00:08:48.580
I'm wondering if I should delete the picture.

00:08:48.580 --> 00:08:52.620
I've got more likes than usual,
but I feel conflicted about it.

00:08:52.620 --> 00:08:54.120
Do what you want.

00:08:54.120 --> 00:08:57.290
It looks like you gave Maeshima some advice.

00:08:57.290 --> 00:08:58.200
You were watching?

00:08:58.200 --> 00:09:00.410
Just a hunch.

00:09:00.410 --> 00:09:05.080
I think we can make use of the upcoming match.

00:09:05.080 --> 00:09:06.790
In our last year of high school,

00:09:06.790 --> 00:09:11.080
we finally have a team that seriously
has a chance at winning nationals.

00:09:11.080 --> 00:09:13.990
But Shinozaki switched to team skating.

00:09:13.990 --> 00:09:17.950
How does this team stack up against
a team with Shinozaki on it?

00:09:17.950 --> 00:09:20.910
I think it's a good litmus test for that.

00:09:20.910 --> 00:09:22.580
It might be too powerful a drug, though.

00:09:22.580 --> 00:09:25.620
Then, we need to seriously try to win.

00:09:25.620 --> 00:09:27.830
Yeah, of course.

00:09:32.200 --> 00:09:34.790
All right, good job, everyone!

00:09:34.790 --> 00:09:35.740
With the measurement device,

00:09:35.740 --> 00:09:38.700
we can get a general idea of
how many points this routine got.

00:09:38.700 --> 00:09:40.620
Let's go back now and analyze it.

00:09:40.620 --> 00:09:43.830
Was there anything that bothered
you guys, Hajime? Susumu?

00:09:46.580 --> 00:09:49.410
All right, it sounds like someone's
reserved this space after us.

00:09:49.410 --> 00:09:51.830
Let's get out of here.

00:09:51.830 --> 00:09:55.200
Even though they're my own kids,
those moves were astonishing.

00:09:55.200 --> 00:09:59.620
I'm glad they improved enough
to make it for their last year, though.

00:09:59.620 --> 00:10:02.330
It's been a while, but it might
be possible to win nationals again...

00:10:08.160 --> 00:10:10.120
Thanks a lot for this, Kuonji.

00:10:10.120 --> 00:10:14.740
The editor-in-chief was also happy that
we could do an exclusive on your practice.

00:10:14.740 --> 00:10:18.700
I owe a lot to Mr. Terasawa,
so it was the least I could do.

00:10:18.700 --> 00:10:22.240
This skating arena is even used
for world championships, right?

00:10:22.240 --> 00:10:26.580
Shinozaki switched to team skating,
so I've lost some motivation,

00:10:26.580 --> 00:10:29.490
and I thought it'd be perfect
for getting me fired up again.

00:10:29.490 --> 00:10:31.860
That's Japan's next ace for you!

00:10:30.940 --> 00:10:33.370
I don't remember asking you to come here.

00:10:33.370 --> 00:10:36.490
Don't say that. We're friends, aren't we?

00:10:36.490 --> 00:10:39.370
I know! You can come watch
our practice next time.

00:10:39.370 --> 00:10:41.240
That's not the issue here.

00:10:41.240 --> 00:10:43.740
Same for you guys, right?

00:10:43.740 --> 00:10:45.080
Hey, don't decide on your own--

00:10:45.080 --> 00:10:46.740
What's going on?

00:10:46.740 --> 00:10:49.660
These are all teams from
last year's Grand Prix finals...

00:10:49.660 --> 00:10:51.410
What're they about to do?

00:10:51.410 --> 00:10:53.370
And Shinozaki's here, too...

00:10:53.370 --> 00:10:55.490
Sorry, sorry!

00:10:55.490 --> 00:10:58.450
I got too excited while practicing...

00:10:58.450 --> 00:11:00.990
Well, wanna get started?

00:11:13.160 --> 00:11:15.950
Hm? Why are there so many people here?

00:11:20.160 --> 00:11:21.450
Hey, Tomo.

00:11:21.450 --> 00:11:23.290
I heard about this and came to watch!

00:11:23.290 --> 00:11:25.740
What's going on?

00:11:25.740 --> 00:11:31.580
U-Um, well, I live next door
to Himuro from St. Clavis,

00:11:31.580 --> 00:11:34.330
and we were on the same team
in middle school, so...

00:11:34.330 --> 00:11:36.200
What did you do?!

00:11:36.200 --> 00:11:37.370
S-Sorry!

00:11:37.370 --> 00:11:39.200
Next time, steal some intel about them.

00:11:39.200 --> 00:11:40.370
What...?

00:11:40.370 --> 00:11:42.990
Anyway, this practice isn't open to the public.

00:11:42.990 --> 00:11:44.290
Sorry, but will you please leave?

00:11:44.290 --> 00:11:47.040
It's fine to let them watch, isn't it?

00:11:47.040 --> 00:11:48.910
Right, Shinozaki?

00:11:50.620 --> 00:11:51.790
It's okay, right?

00:11:51.790 --> 00:11:54.540
If we stop them, you'd just
be less fired up, right?

00:11:54.540 --> 00:11:56.330
You know me too well.

00:11:56.330 --> 00:11:57.870
Coach!

00:11:57.870 --> 00:11:59.200
Do what you want.

00:11:59.200 --> 00:12:03.080
Just make sure you finish
before our reserved time runs out.

00:12:03.080 --> 00:12:04.950
You heard him.

00:12:04.950 --> 00:12:06.200
All right! Then--

00:12:06.200 --> 00:12:07.540
Wait.

00:12:07.540 --> 00:12:08.740
Fine.

00:12:08.740 --> 00:12:11.490
In exchange, we'll be the ones to go first.

00:12:11.490 --> 00:12:13.910
It ended up like this because of your actions.

00:12:13.910 --> 00:12:17.120
I'll have you give us that much.

00:12:17.120 --> 00:12:18.620
He's too nice.

00:12:18.620 --> 00:12:22.870
Is he letting Shima and his team rest
a little since they're all sweaty?

00:12:22.870 --> 00:12:26.870
It's so they can't complain later
when the results come out.

00:12:26.870 --> 00:12:30.620
Besides, if we skate first,
the ice will be smoother.

00:12:30.620 --> 00:12:32.740
Let's leave it at that.

00:12:32.740 --> 00:12:36.370
You haven't forgotten what's at stake, have you?

00:12:36.370 --> 00:12:37.990
Of course not!

00:12:40.120 --> 00:12:42.200
A real competition after practice, huh?

00:12:42.200 --> 00:12:43.700
Let's watch, too.

00:12:43.700 --> 00:12:44.990
Huh? But--

00:12:44.990 --> 00:12:48.200
Shinozaki deems this practice worth watching.

00:12:48.200 --> 00:12:51.200
It might be useful for my performance.

00:12:51.200 --> 00:12:54.950
If it lives up to my expectations, that is.

00:12:54.950 --> 00:12:58.740
I heard you were coaching a
high school team. So you're at this school?

00:12:58.740 --> 00:12:59.740
Mr. Miura...

00:12:59.740 --> 00:13:05.450
I'm here today as the reporter assigned
to cover Japan's next ace, Noa Kuonji.

00:13:05.450 --> 00:13:08.490
How's it going? Are you
having fun being a coach?

00:13:08.490 --> 00:13:12.490
I haven't retired yet.

00:13:12.490 --> 00:13:13.830
I know.

00:13:20.790 --> 00:13:22.040
They're starting.

00:13:29.370 --> 00:13:32.410
They're doing last year's routine
like they said they would, huh?

00:13:32.410 --> 00:13:35.120
They arranged it for three people, though.

00:13:47.910 --> 00:13:52.870
Amazing. Their moves are sharp,
polished, and expressive.

00:13:56.080 --> 00:13:59.910
Wow! To land a quadruple easily like that.

00:13:59.910 --> 00:14:02.080
Because the timing of it was so close,

00:14:02.080 --> 00:14:04.790
the audience can't take their eyes off it.

00:14:04.790 --> 00:14:07.410
That Kiriyama's been practicing.

00:14:07.410 --> 00:14:12.040
If they'd done this last year,
we might not have won nationals.

00:14:12.040 --> 00:14:15.370
To raise the standard this much
in such a short time.

00:14:15.370 --> 00:14:18.240
That guy's pretty good, too.

00:14:18.240 --> 00:14:20.740
Now, to finish it off--

00:14:36.370 --> 00:14:39.580
This is better than I expected.

00:14:38.950 --> 00:14:40.910
Terauchi T

00:14:38.950 --> 00:14:39.950
Calculating...

00:14:41.040 --> 00:14:43.620
Wow! We did pretty good.

00:14:43.620 --> 00:14:45.450
This is nothing to get excited about.

00:14:45.450 --> 00:14:47.950
Our score didn't improve
as much as I thought it would.

00:14:47.950 --> 00:14:51.910
Oh my, you set your sights on
a pretty high goal, huh?

00:14:51.910 --> 00:14:56.410
It's 5.5 points higher than
if our score at last year's nationals

00:14:56.410 --> 00:14:59.040
was recalculated for three people.

00:14:59.040 --> 00:15:02.700
Shima and the others must
be feeling the pressure...

00:15:03.700 --> 00:15:06.120
Or not, it seems.

00:15:06.120 --> 00:15:08.830
Huh? Isn't that Kensei Maeshima?

00:15:08.830 --> 00:15:11.080
Has he returned to skating?

00:15:11.080 --> 00:15:12.620
How is he?

00:15:12.620 --> 00:15:13.450
Who knows?

00:15:13.450 --> 00:15:14.740
You don't know?

00:15:14.740 --> 00:15:17.160
I haven't taught him anything...

00:15:21.080 --> 00:15:23.700
Now, let's see what you've got.

00:15:23.700 --> 00:15:25.790
You understand, right, Maeshima?

00:15:25.790 --> 00:15:28.290
Based on this result, you could
be dropping out of school.

00:15:35.580 --> 00:15:37.620
Maeshima's lead, as expected, huh?

00:15:44.700 --> 00:15:47.120
Huh? He's lead, too?

00:15:47.120 --> 00:15:48.700
They don't have a wing?

00:15:48.700 --> 00:15:49.870
No...

00:15:56.330 --> 00:15:57.160
Wha...?!

00:15:57.160 --> 00:15:58.790
Could this be...?

00:15:58.790 --> 00:16:02.240
Man, we had a tough time
trying to decide on positions.

00:16:02.240 --> 00:16:04.160
Everyone wanted to be lead.

00:16:04.160 --> 00:16:07.620
Technically, we'd need to have
at least one wing and one guard,

00:16:07.620 --> 00:16:09.830
but since this is a three-person team,

00:16:09.830 --> 00:16:12.830
I thought, why not make them all leads?

00:16:12.830 --> 00:16:15.620
I don't think it's against the rules.

00:16:15.620 --> 00:16:18.200
I've considered having three leads for a while.

00:16:18.200 --> 00:16:22.160
I'd wanted to keep it as
our secret weapon at nationals,

00:16:22.160 --> 00:16:26.330
but after seeing Shinozaki
that day, I changed my mind.

00:16:26.330 --> 00:16:30.330
If I'm serious about beating him,
this is no time to be putting on airs.

00:16:30.330 --> 00:16:33.540
It grates that he seems to have noticed, though.

00:16:35.490 --> 00:16:36.620
Oh!

00:16:36.620 --> 00:16:38.080
Crap...

00:16:44.580 --> 00:16:45.950
Huh?

00:16:45.950 --> 00:16:47.660
They've increased the difficulty level.

00:16:47.660 --> 00:16:50.410
Jonouchi and Himekawa were late just now.

00:16:54.740 --> 00:16:59.490
Their movements just now didn't
seem like they went as planned...

00:16:59.490 --> 00:17:02.790
That mongrel, I told him
not to get carried away!

00:17:02.790 --> 00:17:05.790
This feeling of speed, the tension of a match--

00:17:05.790 --> 00:17:07.910
This is super fun!

00:17:07.910 --> 00:17:10.740
This guy's moves are too
different from practice!

00:17:11.790 --> 00:17:14.040
I can do it. I can fly!

00:17:14.040 --> 00:17:18.370
Faster, longer, bigger!

00:17:18.370 --> 00:17:19.950
Stop messing around, bastard!

00:17:19.950 --> 00:17:24.490
Oh? Bigger movements in the second half
to try and get more points, huh?

00:17:24.490 --> 00:17:27.910
You know that's not what that is.

00:17:27.910 --> 00:17:29.120
Amazing...

00:17:29.120 --> 00:17:31.160
Their speed, height, and technical ability.

00:17:31.160 --> 00:17:33.950
They've drastically kicked it
up a notch from the first half.

00:17:33.950 --> 00:17:36.830
But at this rate, will their stamina last?

00:17:49.620 --> 00:17:51.370
Next is the last part!

00:17:51.370 --> 00:17:52.740
Go...!

00:18:13.330 --> 00:18:15.330
You... You idiot!

00:18:15.330 --> 00:18:18.040
Think about us a little, too!

00:18:19.120 --> 00:18:20.870
You little--

00:18:20.870 --> 00:18:23.580
You took the best part for yourself at the end!

00:18:23.580 --> 00:18:25.620
Your skating's amazing!

00:18:28.490 --> 00:18:30.450
It was my best jump ever.

00:18:30.450 --> 00:18:36.490
Was I being pulled? Did he pull me up?

00:18:30.450 --> 00:18:32.830
We won! I'm sure of it!

00:18:32.830 --> 00:18:34.700
We were the best team!

00:18:34.700 --> 00:18:36.490
I said, stop messing around!

00:18:36.490 --> 00:18:37.950
Izumi Himekawa...

00:18:37.950 --> 00:18:42.240
Why didn't anyone notice someone
as skilled as him in middle school?

00:18:42.240 --> 00:18:44.370
The height of that last jump...

00:18:44.370 --> 00:18:46.160
He's the ace of Ionodai.

00:18:46.160 --> 00:18:49.330
I thought we only had
to worry about Shinozaki, but...

00:18:49.330 --> 00:18:50.160
No...

00:18:50.160 --> 00:18:51.370
That's not it.

00:18:51.370 --> 00:18:55.490
We really need to worry about the one
always at the center of the performance--

00:18:55.490 --> 00:18:57.120
Kensei Maeshima.

00:18:58.870 --> 00:19:01.290
That's right.

00:19:01.290 --> 00:19:04.700
Hey, hey! Thanks, thanks--

00:19:04.700 --> 00:19:07.080
You idiot. I told you not to get carried away!

00:19:07.080 --> 00:19:09.990
Looks like I need a stronger chain for you.

00:19:09.990 --> 00:19:11.790
It turned out all right, so it's fine, isn't it?

00:19:11.790 --> 00:19:13.370
It's <i>not</i> "all right"!

00:19:15.370 --> 00:19:16.790
The score's coming!

